## Objective
- Implement phase-062 in the redblue checkout (`/home/runner/work/rbops/rbops/redblue`): add `.debug <expr|file>` entering a debug sub-REPL with `.watch`, `.stack`, `.locals`, observe-only semantics, exiting with the parent session untouched (DoD tests for stack order, watch change-reporting, locals frame isolation, parent byte-identity).
- Follow the fixed pipeline: reproduce → one failing targeted test → smallest fix → edge tests → four gates (`cargo fmt --all -- --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test --all-targets`, `../rbops/verify.sh "phase-062"`) → write `phases/phase-062/REPORT.md`, then say DONE.

## Important Details
- Hard rules (AGENTS.md): never touch `.github/workflows/`, `rbops/`, `rbops/phases.json`, `.opencode/agent/`; never weaken gates/tests (strengthening/adding rows to existing tests is allowed); no `#[ignore]`/`allow(clippy::`/skips; no long local `cargo build`; write only inside project (scratch: `./target/tmp/`); `must_touch: [src/]`; quota: ≥3 new `#[test]`, ≥1 `edge_*`, ≥1 asserting a failure, zero newly-failing pre-existing tests; describe `../rbops/verify.sh` behavior, don't paste outputs in REPORT.
- Budget noted: reproduce by 2 min, first test by 5, first edit by 10 (reproduce done, first test written and red-then-green done).
- Reproduction (done): `printf '.watch x\n.stack\n.locals\n.debug 1 + 1\n:quit\n' | ./target/debug/rb` → `Unknown command 'watch'/'stack'/'locals'`; `.debug 1 + 1` ignored its argument and printed `Debugger: 0 breakpoint(s) set...`. Evidence text claiming `.debug` absent was stale — note staleness in REPORT/FINDINGS.
- Design decisions finalized:
  - `commands.rs`: variants `Debug(String)` (names `["debug"]`, usage `Some("<expression|file>")`, `optional_argument: true` → bare `.debug` = `Debug("")`), `Watch(String)` (usage `Some("<expression>")`, required), `Stack`, `Locals`, `Back` (name `["back"]` only; `exit` taken, `leave` not added). Parent-prompt answer for Watch/Stack/Locals/Back: `"No debug session is open. Type .debug <expression|file> to open one."` (`NO_DEBUG_SESSION` const).
  - `argument_text`: added `| ReplCommand::Debug(value) | ReplCommand::Watch(value)`.
  - `.watch` semantics: registration = parse-only (parse failure → `failure_line`, NOT registered); `last: None` until first successful eval which seeds a silent BASELINE (no creation report); thereafter report `watch {source} = {value}` only when value != last; eval error each step → `watch {source}: {first line of error Display}`. No NaN comparator needed: `Value::number` refuses non-finite (`0/0` is a Runtime error), equality via `PartialEq`.
  - Scratch watch VM: hook-closure-owned `Vm::new()` with `ask_questions(true)` (refuses effectful builtins), bindings overwritten per step via new `Vm::observe_bindings(scopes, globals)` (also resets `statement_depth`, drains output). No step-budget reset needed (MAX_STEPS = 32_000_000; parent never resets either — consistent).
  - `.stack` format: `"Call stack ({} frame{s}):"` + `"  {name}"` lines, outermost first; empty/not-observed → `"No live frames."`. `.locals`: not-observed → `"No live frames."`; empty → `"Locals: (no bindings)"`; else `"Locals:"` + `"  name = value"` sorted by name.
  - `.locals` rule: scopes[scope_base..] innermost-wins; if `frame_writes` is `None` (top level) → all program globals (`is_program_name` filtered); if `Some` → only globals in that frame's writes (sorted). `DebugEvent::frame_locals()` method added in debugger.rs (distinct from `Frame::capture`).
  - `.debug` entry: arg ends `.rb` → `std::fs::read_to_string` (read error line `"Error: cannot read '{arg}': {err}"`, session still enters, banner first); else run as code. `.debug <arg>` while ALREADY in session → runs arg in current session (re-entry semantics; bare `.debug` inside → `ALREADY_IN_SESSION` message).
  - `.back` clears `self.debug_repl = None` silently; driver lines contract: first line may be `.debug`; non-`.debug` line before any session → `NO_DEBUG_SESSION`.
  - Sub-REPL commands not supported (Quit/Clear/Load/etc.) → `SUB_ONLY_MESSAGE`; `Help` → `SUB_HELP` (one line listing the five sub commands); `Unknown` → parent's wording verbatim; `MissingArgument` → `Usage: :{command} {usage}` (parent's format).
  - Sub has its own `buffer: Vec<String>` (parent's `multiline_buffer`/`in_multiline` untouched); `prompt()` = `"debug> "` or `"..  {n} "`; reuses `Repl::exceeds_block_limits`, `Repl::needs_continuation`, `BLOCK_REPORT_LINES`, `MAX_BLOCK_LINES`/`MAX_BLOCK_BYTES` (private items of parent module, visible to child `debug_repl`).
  - session_loop: sub branch placed right after empty-input check, BEFORE history.push — `if self.debug_repl.is_some() { for line in self.debug_line(input) { println } continue; }` → parent history/transcript/definitions/last_output/tutorials untouched by sub lines; entry `.debug` line itself IS recorded by session_loop (document in REPORT).
  - Driver returns `Vec<String>` (tests read lines, not stdout). Program output (take_output) → `= value` (painted `Paint::Result`) or `Error: {render_error}` (painted inside render_error) → then drained watch reports. Sub `_` stored in `DebugRepl.variables`.
  - `frame_writes` only recorded on set_var's globals fall-through via `last_mut()` (top level = empty stack = untracked); `bind_constant`/`bind_module_name` not tracked (acceptable, document).
  - session_names union: while sub active, `Repl::session_names` also extends with `debug.session_names()` (affects completer snapshot only).
  - GLUE VISIBILITY: `impl Repl` block lives in `debug_repl.rs`; its methods (`debug_session`, `enter_debug`, `debug_line`) must be `pub(super)` so `repl/mod.rs` can call them; `DebugRepl` methods `session_names`, `prompt`, `report_unclosed_block`, `watch`, `stack_lines`, `locals_lines`, `push_line`, `run`, `new` are `pub(super)` (or private where same-module). Constants: `NO_DEBUG_SESSION` is `pub(super)` (used in mod.rs), others private.
- Verified facts: only ONE `DebugEvent {` construction (interpreter.rs:1565 `debug_before`); no existing test references `.debug`/`:debug`/`debug_mode`/"Debugger:" output; completer/highlight have no exhaustive `ReplCommand` matches (only `handle_command`); `call_user_function` is the single choke point (callers at 2234, 2286 callbacks, 2422 object methods); `Style` is `Copy`; `SessionNames = Rc<RefCell<Vec<String>>>`; `LineSource`/`Line` are pub; `Error::message()` is pub; `Vm::new()` = `new_in(".")`; `back` is a Redblue keyword (`GiveBack`) but command parsing is sigil-prefixed so no conflict; `debug_before` fires BEFORE `charge_step`; MAX_STEPS default 32_000_000.
- Intended output message texts (final): `BANNER`, `SUB_HELP`, `SUB_ONLY_MESSAGE`, `ALREADY_IN_SESSION` — as written in debug_repl.rs (see file).

